WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.388
This example combines normalization and fallback
logic We want the first usable

00:00:05.412 --> 00:00:09.262
contact method but an empty email or a string
containing only spaces

00:00:09.288 --> 00:00:13.862
should not block the fallback Each contact value is
trimmed and NULLIF

00:00:13.888 --> 00:00:18.762
converts an empty result to NULL COALESCE then
chooses the first available

00:00:18.775 --> 00:00:23.988
value The order expresses priority email then mobile
then home then a

00:00:24.012 --> 00:00:29.362
final label Run the query and inspect the edge cases
Robert Lee

00:00:29.388 --> 00:00:33.325
and Lisa Ray should fall back to home phone Maria
Torres should

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:38.325
use mobile because her email contains only spaces
Andre Green should receive

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:40.400
the final No contact provided label
